prise, surprise! A complexity science view of the unexpected</article-title><source>Health Care Management Review</source><year>2003</year><volume>28</volume><fpage>266</fpage><lpage>278</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12940348</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B26"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>McKelvey</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Avoiding complexity catastrophe in co-evolutionary pockets: Strategies for rugged landscapes</article-title><source>Organization Science</source><year>1999</year><volume>10</volume><fpage>294</fpage><lpage>321</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B27"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Waldrop</surname><given-names>MM</given-names></name></person-group><source>Complexity: The emerging science at the edge of order and chaos</source><year>1992</year><publisher-name>New York, NY: Touchstone by Simon and Schuster Inc</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B28"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Allen</surname><given-names>PM</given-names></name><name><surname>Strathern</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Baldwin</surname><given-names>JS</given-names></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>McDaniel RR Jr, Driebe DJ</surname></name></person-group><article-title>The evolutionary complexity of social economic systems: The inevitability of uncertainty and surprise</article-title><source>Uncertainty and Surprise in Complex Systems</source><year>2005</year><publisher-name>Berlin: Springer-Verlag</publisher-name><fpage>31</fpage><lpage>50</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B29"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lammers</surname><given-names>JC</given-names></name><name><surname>Barbour</surname><given-names>JB</given-names></name>